WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.277
- So what were you like as a kid,

00:00:01.277 --> 00:00:03.210
were you both talkative?

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.980
'Cause you're both, even
though you might not

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.813
be a stand up comedian,

00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:07.610
you're a very comedic
actor, so were y'all,

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.520
and you're very friendly.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.890
Were y'all both like this as kids?

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.640
- Where'd you grow up?
- Pittsburgh.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.900
- Oh, got you.
- You?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.150
- Long Island.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.560
- Everyone cool is from Long Island.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.680
(applause)

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.513
- Really?

00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:18.540
- That's cool.
- I didn't know that.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.127
- Yeah, Long Island, New
Jersey, that whole area.

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:21.560
But were y'all always this talkative?

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.363
Or were you introverts when you were kids?

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:24.750
- I was talkative.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.380
My brother and I, my brother
Eliot is also a comedian.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.246
We would make sketch videos for hours,

00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:31.079
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:31.958
and hours and hours.

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:35.410
I've always been a comedy
nerd, and that's it.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.540
- That's awesome.
- That's all I am.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.650
- Were you always this talkative?

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.582
You knew everyone, right off the bat?

00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:39.950
- No, no.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:44.080
I was very, I was sort of,
I needed to be a good boy

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.710
in school, I made good grades,
and there was kind of a,

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.240
I was, you know, properly--

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.480
- [Kelly] Strict household?
- Huh?

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.080
- You said good little boy,
was it a strict household?

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.960
- They were kind of
strict, there was some kind

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.330
of serious demand that we be well behaved

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.820
in one area or another
and in school certainly

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.370
so I was kinda constrained.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.850
So I, it was kind of an
outlet when I found myself,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.380
I had to find my voice by
and by, as I'm still doing.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.690
But I remember, I had a talent
for drawing and painting

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.620
and my dad would take us

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.620
to this special art class, me every week.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.480
And waiting outside the
Carnegie Melon Museum,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.765
the Carnegie Museum.
- Wow.

00:01:21.765 --> 00:01:25.250
- He hadn't shown up yet
and I would do this thing,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.340
that I can't believe I
did, I was like 11 or 12,

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.500
I would see people and
then pretend to know them.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.130
To go, "Oh my gosh, look who it is!"

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.392
- I think there's a word for
that, it's called stalker.

00:01:38.392 --> 00:01:40.976
- It's strange.
- That's strange.

00:01:40.976 --> 00:01:41.809
You were 14?

00:01:41.809 --> 00:01:43.370
- Yeah, 14 or 11 or 12
or something like that.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.870
- What a bizarre level of
agency, to grown ups, to adults.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.580
- Do you think it was to make
you feel more comfortable

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.305
that you were alone in that moment?

00:01:49.305 --> 00:01:50.138
- I don't know, I think was me--

00:01:50.138 --> 00:01:52.490
- Wow, someone goes to therapy, okay.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.460
Okay, I see you Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.293
- Hashtag truth.

